& [Term_Acquisition] means one later producer event
  + requires separately authorized physical observation under one exact scanner contract
  + begins and ends in actual producer control flow
  + is not instantiated by a form, identity, supplied carrier, test fixture, or validation result
  - not: a request, JSON object, logical row, digest computation, or reconciliation operand

& [Term_AcquisitionIdentity] means bounded logical correlation in this profile
  + binds declarations about one claimed event across forms
  + uses exact nonzero u64 equality and inequality
  + is stable in serialization and finite in representation
  - not: generated uniqueness, collision freedom, temporal order, producer identity, nonce, proof, or capability

& [Term_Distinct] means exact identity inequality plus role separation
  + first identity differs from second identity
  + each role owns its own complete lineage value
  + no one lineage instance may satisfy both semantic roles
  - not: different field names, different object addresses, different digests, or different caller ordinals alone

& [Term_Scope] means the complete comparison product
  + includes every root, profile, encoding, limit, policy, predecessor, and receipt-relation coordinate selected by canonical SJS
  + equality is structural equality of every coordinate
  + missing or unequal coordinates deny common scope
  - not: a label, hash without governed grammar, optional subset, wildcard, or caller-asserted equivalence

& [Term_CompleteClaimed] means one closed claim disposition
  + declares that the claim author presents the lineage as complete for pure reasoning
  + permits validation of the requested conjunction
  + carries no producer witness or runtime lifecycle state
  - not: completed observation, successful traversal, fault absence, admission, proof, or trust

& [Term_Lineage] means retained derivation ancestry
  + owns one complete current ordered digest carrier
  + thereby retains the current assembly carrier and its transitive supplied inputs
  + permits independent current rederivation and inspection
  - not: physical origin, same-handle continuity, observation time, database lookup, or authority chain

& [Term_Carrier] means bounded owned semantic input or output
  + carries exact fields and transitive pure ancestry under a named current profile
  + can be validated and rederived without external state
  + remains supplied until a later producer binds physical provenance
  - not: evidence that the world produced its contents

& [Term_Current] means exact governed profile and implementation binding
  + requires the named profile, canonical authority, signature, and bound module hash
  + invalidates processing on drift
  - not: most recent wall-clock version, fresh world state, or automatic upgrade

& [Term_OrderedPair] means explicit semantic roles
  + FirstAcquisition and SecondAcquisition are named roles over two distinct lineages
  + pair ownership alone imposes no temporal fact
  + the causal relation separately binds the role identities
  - not: vector position, JSON key order, left and right, ascending number, or lexical order

& [Term_FirstCompletionStrictlyPrecedesSecondStart] means one claimed causal edge
  + source role is first acquisition completion
  + target role is second acquisition start
  + direction and endpoint identities are exact
  + pure validation establishes only internal coherence of the declaration
  - not: a clock observation, duration, freshness bound, concurrency exclusion, or proof that either event occurred

& [Term_Rederive] means execute the current pure transform again
  + validates the complete nested carrier before computing its derived subject
  + compares computed and retained derived values under exact current rules
  + reads no external state
  - not: trust copied digest text, reconstruct physical acquisition, or refresh a carrier

& [Term_Equal] means exact current reconciliation disposition
  + both independently rederived canonical commitments match under exact common scope
  + is a necessary subordinate condition for requested repeated-equality evidence
  - not: object identity, same acquisition, quiescence, atomicity, no intermediate change, no later change, or snapshot

& [Term_Different] means valid non-equality disposition
  + both carriers and reconciliation may be structurally valid
  + denies the requested repeated-equality ClaimOnly result
  + remains distinct from malformed input or rederivation fault
  - not: scanner failure, corruption, maliciousness, or proof of when change occurred

& [Term_ClaimOnly] means explicit lowest provenance grade
  + the complete declared conjunction passed pure structural and relational checks
  + current carrier rederivation and Equal reconciliation succeeded
  + complete inspectable lineage is retained
  - not: actual acquisition, production admission, issued evidence, receipt, current truth, or authorization

& [Term_OutputOnly] means production non-decodability
  + a governed pure function is the only production construction route
  + fields remain private and inspection uses immutable getters or serialization
  + Deserialize and Default are absent
  - not: secret, opaque to audit, cryptographically authentic, or physically authoritative

& [Term_ProductionAdmission] means later capability-bound provenance transition
  + may occur only after actual observation under separately signed M2C authority
  + must bind producer identity, collision domain, control-flow order, and observation output
  + is completely absent from profile 0.1
  - not: private Rust fields, crate visibility, successful validation, or a convention

& [Term_Synthetic] means compile-time test-only construction
  + exists solely inside cfg(test) or through public pure transforms over declared supplied data
  + must retain claim vocabulary and cannot enter an admitted production surface
  - not: mock proof, trusted acquisition, equivalent provenance, or a production bypass

& [Term_Strict] means closed and fail closed
  + exact profiles and variants only
  + unknown fields, aliases, defaults, omitted coordinates, and compatibility fallbacks are rejected
  + every bound and relation is checked before output
  - not: inflexible prose, accidental implementation coupling, or authority widening

& [Term_Bounded] means finite before work begins
  + cardinalities and scalar ranges have declared maxima
  + nested carrier complexity is inherited from current enforced limits
  + arithmetic and diagnostic sizes are checked
  - not: merely small in current tests, memory-success dependent, or post-allocation rejection only

& [Term_AtomicFault] means one complete bounded denial
  + identifies one closed fault category and bounded field/message locus
  + returns no partial result or admitted provenance
  + Different remains a comparison disposition mapped separately when repeated equality is requested
  - not: transaction atomicity, filesystem atomicity, snapshot, panic, or multi-error accumulation

& [Term_Proof] remains grade specific
  + SJS proof establishes artifact and implementation conformance only after signature
  + pure test proof establishes deterministic behavior over supplied inputs
  + physical proof requires later authorized observation and fixture governance
  + no proof grade substitutes for another
  - not: a generic success label transferable across authority boundaries

& [Term_NoEffect] means no external-state interaction
  + no platform call, filesystem access, clock, randomness, process, environment, network, persistence, database, Git runtime, model, or tool operation
  + no acquisition, admission, issuance, consumption, mutation, seal, cleanup, promotion, neural, distributed, or FPGA action
  + pure CPU and bounded owned-memory transforms remain permitted only after implementation signature
  - not: present implementation authority or permission to execute unsigned code

& [ForbiddenSubstitutions] are exact
  + logical identity never substitutes for actual event identity
  + CompleteClaimed never substitutes for completed acquisition
  + carrier ancestry never substitutes for physical provenance
  + role mapping never substitutes for causal proof
  + Equal never substitutes for repeated acquisition evidence
  + ClaimOnly never substitutes for issued evidence
  + output-only never substitutes for authentic
  + private fields never substitute for capability
  + test-only never substitutes for production-admitted
  + receipt-form validity never substitutes for receipt issuance or present truth

